# WS223 transitive dependency lock — compiler input.
#
# This file mirrors the DIRECT dependency ranges declared in
# `pyproject.toml` ([project].dependencies + dev/api/openai extras) plus the
# audit-tool set from `requirements/quality-tools.verified-upstream.txt` and
# `jsonschema` (imported by qualification/harness.py; previously only
# transitively present, now an explicit input with provenance recorded here).
#
# DO NOT EDIT the compiled `requirements/lock.txt` by hand. Regenerate with:
#
#   python -m venv /tmp/ws223-locktools/.venv
#   /tmp/ws223-locktools/.venv/bin/pip install "pip-tools==7.6.1"
#   /tmp/ws223-locktools/.venv/bin/pip-compile \
#       --generate-hashes --resolver=backtracking --strip-extras --allow-unsafe \
#       --output-file=requirements/lock.txt requirements/lock.in
#
# (--allow-unsafe so the setuptools build backend is pinned like any other
# artifact; pip itself is pinned because pip-api genuinely requires it.)
#
# (Exact reproduction also recorded in requirements/LOCK_PROVENANCE.json.)
# Then verify with:
#
#   python scripts/verify_dependency_lock.py --lock requirements/lock.txt

